Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error frame with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Incremental Schema Mismatch Error",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["invalid_schema"]
    },
    "hint": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "checkpoint_cursor": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "checkpoint_version": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "resume_token": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "A resume token that can be used to resume streaming from the last successful checkpoint."
        },
        "kv_crc": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "A checksum of the key-value (KV) data associated with the last successful checkpoint. This checksum is used to verify the integrity of the KV data during streaming resume attempts."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed as a checksum of the key-value (KV) data associated with the last successful checkpoint. This checksum is used to verify the integrity of the KV data during streaming resume attempts. The specific algorithm used to compute the `kv_crc` value is not specified in the context provided
